Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: keep uevents when a property is temporarily unavailable

The Qualcomm battery manager returns -EAGAIN while its firmware service
is starting. Aborting the entire power-supply event drops the device name,
type and any other available properties, and makes initramfs udev trigger
report a failure for each supply.

Treat temporary unavailability like other missing properties when
building the event. Keep -EAGAIN for direct property reads and thermal
consumers, and keep propagating transport and allocation failures.

---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_sysfs.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_sysfs.c
@@ -539,10 +539,11 @@
 	dev_attr = &pwr_attr->dev_attr;
 
 	ret = power_supply_format_property((struct device *)dev, true, dev_attr, prop_buf);
-	if (ret == -ENODEV || ret == -ENODATA || ret == -EINVAL) {
+	if (ret == -ENODEV || ret == -ENODATA || ret == -EINVAL || ret == -EAGAIN) {
 		/*
 		 * When a battery is absent, we expect -ENODEV. Don't abort;
-		 * send the uevent with at least the PRESENT=0 property
+		 * send the uevent with at least the PRESENT=0 property. Also allow
+		 * properties which are temporarily unavailable during initialization.
 		 */
 		return 0;
 	}
